<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Jan inflation seen falling to 2.12 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>Belgian Jan inflation seen falling to 2.12 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian inflation was seen falling to 2.12 percent year-on-year in January from December's 2.53 percent, according to a Reuters poll of Belgian economists. Inflation month-on-month was seen at 0.5 percent.</p>
<p>Following is a summary of economists' forecasts for January inflation.</p>
<p>    Analysts		 Mo/Mo	Yr/Yr</p>
<p>    BBL			0.6	   2.2</p>
<p>    CCB/Gemeentekrediet  0.4	   2.0</p>
<p>    Generale Bank	  0.5	   2.1</p>
<p>    J.P.Morgan	     0.6	   2.2</p>
<p>    Kredietbank	    0.5	   2.1</p>
<p>Average (vs last month)  0.52 (0.18) 2.12 (2.53)</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
